# Raw upstream downloads: reproducible by re-running collect.py (and, for the
# ICRISAT blob specifically, icrisat.load_raw()). The training tables and
# model JSONs are the artefacts worth tracking, not the bytes they came from.
#
# The ICRISAT raw JSON is kept out of git for another reason too: fetching it
# has proven unreliable (the upstream server drops most transfers before
# completion), so the cached copy in a contributor's own cache/ is valuable
# precisely because it does not need to be re-fetched -- but that is a local
# convenience, not something to commit.
cache/

# Date-stamped live pulls from predict.py, one per point per run day.
cache/live_*.csv
__pycache__/
